<urn:cpi:source:14:90> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 90" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:14> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "9"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "4"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 9 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "ed2c3ab4351c2b264e5cc27e6c013de3d4d8cee114f40e2c33328172889e1df5"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """9. 9. Reporting and Transparency
The Bank is committed to maintaining transparency and accountability in the management of its Covenant Packages. To this
end, the Credit Monitoring Team must prepare and distribute regular reports on covenant compliance, breaches, and corrective
actions to key stakeholders, including the WCRC, senior management, and the Board of Directors.
The Credit Monitoring Team must prepare a monthly Covenant Compliance Report, which summarizes the results of all
covenant tests conducted during the month, including any breaches, waivers, or amendments. The report must also highlight
any trends or emerging risks in the Bank’s wholesale credit portfolio. The monthly report must be distributed to the WCRC and
senior management within 10 business days of the end of the month.
In addition to the monthly report, the Credit Monitoring Team must prepare a quarterly Covenant Risk Report for the Board of
Directors. This report must provide a high-level overview of the Bank’s covenant monitoring processes, the effectiveness of its
controls, and any material risks or issues identified. The quarterly report must also include a summary of all waivers,
amendments, and exceptions approved during the quarter, along with their rationale and impact on the Bank’s risk profile.
The Bank must also maintain a centralized dashboard that provides real-time visibility into the status of all Covenant Packages
across its wholesale credit portfolio. The dashboard must be accessible to the WCRC, senior management, and other
authorized stakeholders and must include key metrics such as the number of active covenants, the frequency of breaches, and
the average time to resolve breaches.
The Bank’s internal audit function must conduct an annual review of the Covenant Package monitoring and reporting processes
to ensure compliance with this Policy and the effectiveness of the Bank’s controls. The findings of the internal audit must be
reported to the WCRC and the Board of Directors, along with any recommendations for improvement."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "4.2"^^xsd:string .

<urn:cpi:source:14:91> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 91" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:14> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "9"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "4"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 10 ;
