    cpi:version "4.2"^^xsd:string .

<urn:cpi:source:14:92> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 92" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:14> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "10"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "4"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 10 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "ed2c3ab4351c2b264e5cc27e6c013de3d4d8cee114f40e2c33328172889e1df5"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """10. 10. Policy Review and Updates
This Policy must be reviewed annually by the Credit Policy Team to ensure that it remains aligned with the Bank’s risk appetite,
regulatory requirements, and industry best practices. The annual review must include an assessment of the Policy’s
effectiveness in mitigating covenant-related risks, as well as any gaps or areas for improvement identified through the Bank’s
monitoring and reporting processes.
The Credit Policy Team must solicit feedback from key stakeholders, including the WCRC, Credit Approval Team, Credit
Monitoring Team, Legal Team, and Relationship Managers, as part of the annual review. This feedback must be documented
and considered in the preparation of any updates or amendments to the Policy.
Any proposed updates or amendments to the Policy must be submitted to the WCRC for review and approval. The WCRC must
assess the impact of the proposed changes on the Bank’s risk management framework and ensure that they are consistent with
the Parent Policy CP-Wholesale-v4.2. Approved updates must be communicated to all relevant stakeholders and implemented
within 30 days of approval.
The Policy must also be updated in response to material changes in the Bank’s risk appetite, regulatory environment, or market
conditions. For example, if the Bank’s risk appetite statement is revised to reflect a more conservative approach to leverage, the
Covenant Package thresholds may need to be adjusted accordingly. Similarly, if new regulatory requirements are introduced
that impact covenant monitoring or reporting, the Policy must be updated to ensure compliance.
The Credit Policy Team is responsible for maintaining a version control log for this Policy, which must document all updates,
amendments, and reviews, including the date of the change, the rationale, and the approval authority. The version control log
must be retained for a minimum of seven years and made available to the Bank’s internal audit function and regulatory
authorities upon request."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "4.2"^^xsd:string .

