<urn:cpi:source:2:40> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 40" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:2> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "10"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "2"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 10 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "dcf967eb4e6f0aa4101bd1dae53a8260a8cb662e8a45cd6ce883fdd3b766430c"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """10. 10. Policy Review and Updates
The 4.2 Leverage Limits clause is subject to regular review to ensure its continued relevance, effectiveness, and alignment with
the bank’s risk appetite and regulatory requirements. The policy review process is overseen by the Credit Risk Committee
(CRC) and involves input from a range of stakeholders, including the Wholesale Credit Risk team, Industry Risk, Quantitative
Analytics, and Internal Audit.
The policy is reviewed at least annually, with the CRC conducting a comprehensive assessment of its performance, including
an evaluation of leverage limit breaches, the effectiveness of corrective actions, and the adequacy of the quantitative
thresholds. The review also considers changes in the bank’s risk appetite, as well as developments in the regulatory landscape,
such as updates to Basel III or other relevant frameworks.
This clause is synthetic demonstration data, and the review processes described are fictional. They are provided for illustrative
purposes only and do not represent the actual policy review practices of any real financial institution.
In addition to the annual review, the policy may be updated on an ad-hoc basis in response to significant events, such as
material breaches, changes in macroeconomic conditions, or regulatory developments. Ad-hoc updates are subject to the same
approval process as the annual review, with the CRC and Chief Credit Officer (CCO) retaining final authority over any changes.
All updates to the policy are documented in a version control log, which tracks the nature of the changes, the rationale, and the
approval date.
The bank communicates policy updates to all relevant stakeholders through a combination of email notifications, intranet
postings, and training sessions. Relationship managers and credit officers are required to acknowledge receipt of the updated
policy and confirm their understanding of any changes. The bank also maintains a centralized repository of all credit policies,
including historical versions, to ensure transparency and accountability. The next scheduled review for this clause is September"""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "4.2"^^xsd:string .

<urn:cpi:source:2:41> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 41" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:2> ;
