<urn:cpi:source:49:242> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 242" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:49> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "1"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "11"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 1 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "067ea0df55a1950a6f414e2436d7ac36cad81a25ad50f752f9ba8449ed70a5eb"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """1. 1. Purpose
This clause, 2.2 Eligible Collateral, under the parent policy COL-Std-v2.4, establishes the framework for identifying, evaluating,
and accepting collateral as security for credit exposures within the bank. The purpose of this document is to ensure that
collateral used to secure credit facilities meets the bank’s risk appetite, regulatory requirements, and internal standards for
creditworthiness and liquidity. This clause is synthetic demonstration data and does not reflect actual bank policies or practices.
The primary objective is to mitigate credit risk by defining clear criteria for collateral eligibility, valuation methodologies, and
ongoing monitoring requirements. By standardizing these processes, the bank aims to maintain a consistent approach to
collateral management across all business units and jurisdictions. This clause applies to all credit facilities, including loans,
overdrafts, and other extensions of credit, where collateral is pledged as security.
The policy ensures that collateral is sufficient to cover the exposure in the event of default, thereby protecting the bank’s
financial interests. It also aligns with regulatory expectations, such as those outlined in Basel III, which emphasize the
importance of high-quality collateral in reducing risk-weighted assets. The bank’s internal risk management framework further
reinforces these requirements to ensure robustness and compliance.
This clause is designed to provide clarity to credit officers, risk managers, and other stakeholders involved in the collateral
evaluation process. It outlines the roles and responsibilities of each party, ensuring accountability and transparency in
decision-making. The policy also serves as a reference for auditors and regulators, demonstrating the bank’s commitment to
prudent risk management practices.
Finally, this document is intended to be a living policy, subject to periodic review and updates to reflect changes in the bank’s
risk appetite, regulatory environment, or market conditions. The synthetic nature of this data ensures that it can be adapted for
training, testing, or demonstration purposes without compromising real-world policy integrity."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "2.4"^^xsd:string .

