<urn:cpi:source:50:262> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 262" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:50> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "1"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "12"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 1 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "57daf82286a273df900c1ea4ba94e1cc2f901b066d3e1221937e96760ef9739d"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """1. 1. Purpose
The purpose of this Haircuts Clause (Clause 2.3) under the Parent Policy COL-Std-v2.4 is to establish a standardized
framework for applying haircuts to collateral assets accepted by the bank in secured lending transactions. This clause ensures
consistency, risk mitigation, and regulatory compliance in the valuation and acceptance of collateral across all business lines.
Haircuts are critical in accounting for the potential decline in the value of collateral assets due to market volatility, liquidity
constraints, or other risk factors.
This policy is designed to align with the bank’s broader credit risk management objectives, ensuring that collateral values are
conservatively estimated to protect the bank’s financial position. By defining clear haircut parameters, the bank aims to maintain
a buffer against potential losses, thereby safeguarding its capital adequacy and liquidity ratios. This clause is synthetic
demonstration data and does not reflect actual bank policies or practices.
The haircut framework outlined herein applies to all types of collateral, including but not limited to marketable securities, real
estate, inventory, and accounts receivable. Each asset class is subject to specific haircut percentages, which are determined
based on historical volatility, liquidity risk, and market depth. The policy ensures that haircuts are applied uniformly across the
bank’s operations, regardless of the jurisdiction or business unit involved.
This clause also serves to enhance transparency and accountability in the collateral management process. By documenting the
rationale behind haircut percentages and the methodologies used, the bank demonstrates its commitment to robust risk
management practices. This transparency is essential for internal audits, regulatory examinations, and stakeholder confidence.
Finally, the purpose of this clause extends to supporting the bank’s strategic goals by enabling secure lending practices that
balance risk and return. Through the disciplined application of haircuts, the bank can optimize its collateral usage while
maintaining a prudent risk profile. This policy is intended for internal use and is part of a synthetic demonstration dataset."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "2.4"^^xsd:string .

