<urn:cpi:source:57:416> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 416" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:57> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "7"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "19"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 7 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "0171f0f0bb413e95a3c9a8253d8c5f71b9496025d505b0e93709b7366b224fc5"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """7. 7. Monitoring and Validation
The bank’s RWA treatment processes are subject to continuous monitoring and periodic validation to ensure their accuracy,
reliability, and compliance with Basel IV. The Credit Risk Department (CRD) is responsible for monitoring the bank’s RWA
calculations on a daily basis, with a focus on identifying any anomalies, breaches of limits, or deviations from the policy.
Monitoring activities include the review of RWA reports, the validation of input data, and the assessment of model performance.
The policy mandates that the CRD conduct a monthly review of the bank’s RWA portfolio to assess trends, concentrations, and
emerging risks. This review includes an analysis of RWA growth by business unit, sector, and geography, as well as a
comparison of actual RWA against the bank’s internal limits and regulatory requirements. Any material deviations or breaches
must be investigated and reported to the RMC, along with a corrective action plan.
In addition to ongoing monitoring, the policy requires that the bank conduct an annual validation of its RWA methodologies and
models. This validation is performed by an independent team within the CRD and includes a comprehensive assessment of the
accuracy and robustness of the RWA calculations. The validation process involves backtesting the models against historical
data, stress testing the models under adverse scenarios, and benchmarking the results against industry standards.
The policy also requires that the bank’s internal models for PD, LGD, and EAD be validated at least annually. The validation
includes an assessment of the models’ conceptual soundness, data quality, and performance against actual outcomes. Models
that fail to meet the validation criteria must be remediated or replaced within a specified timeframe, typically not exceeding six
months. The results of the validation are documented in a report, which is submitted to the RMC for approval.
This synthetic monitoring and validation section demonstrates how a bank might ensure the integrity of its RWA treatment
processes. It includes fictional frequencies, roles, and methodologies to illustrate the importance of ongoing oversight and
independent validation in maintaining compliance with Basel IV and internal risk management standards."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "Basel IV"^^xsd:string .

<urn:cpi:source:57:417> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 417" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:57> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "7"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "19"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 8 ;
