<urn:cpi:source:69:1560> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 1560" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:69> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "7"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "31"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 7 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "e6bb9031cfd51e60c492e3ee404912c4ccff3400a083ae4d6675fdf73e31d0b9"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """7. 7. Approval Authorities and Delegation
The approval authorities and delegation framework outlined in RAT-1.0 are designed to ensure that credit decisions are made
at the appropriate level of seniority, based on the size, complexity, and risk profile of the exposure. The framework establishes
clear thresholds for approval authority, as well as the circumstances under which delegation or escalation is required.
Credit exposures up to USD 1 million may be approved by a designated Credit Officer within the business unit, provided the
exposure is rated investment-grade (BBB- or higher) and complies with all other underwriting criteria. Exposures between USD"""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "1.0"^^xsd:string .

