<urn:cpi:source:15:96> a cpi:SourcePassage ;
    rdfs:label "Source clause 96" ;
    cpi:SOURCE_IN_VERSION <urn:cpi:version:15> ;
    cpi:clause_reference "2"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:document_reference "5"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:origin "POLICY_SOURCE"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:page 2 ;
    cpi:source_checksum "58065e833dd68879f239c9bc9b41406402af03091875effc1641a6145f3bc489"^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:status "APPROVED" ;
    cpi:synthetic true ;
    cpi:text """2. 2. Scope
This clause applies to all retail credit products originated, renewed, or refinanced under the parent policy CP-Retail-v3.1. It
encompasses unsecured and secured lending, including but not limited to personal loans, auto loans, credit cards, and home
equity lines of credit. The DSCR minimums defined herein are mandatory for all retail borrowers, regardless of their credit tier or
relationship with the bank.
The scope of this clause includes both new applications and existing portfolios. For new applications, DSCR minimums must be
verified during the underwriting process. For existing portfolios, DSCR compliance must be monitored as part of the bank's
ongoing credit review process. Any deviations from the established minimums must be documented, justified, and approved
through the exception process outlined in Section 9.
This clause is applicable to all geographic regions and business units where the parent policy CP-Retail-v3.1 is in effect.
However, regional or product-specific adjustments to DSCR minimums may be permitted with the approval of the Chief Risk
Officer (CRO) or their designated delegate. Such adjustments must be documented and communicated to all relevant
stakeholders to ensure consistency in application.
The DSCR minimums apply to all borrowers, including individuals, sole proprietors, and small business entities classified under
the retail segment. For commercial borrowers or those classified under other segments, refer to the respective commercial
credit policies. This clause does not override any legal or regulatory requirements that may impose stricter DSCR thresholds.
Exclusions from this clause include credit products explicitly governed by other policies, such as mortgage lending or
commercial real estate financing. Additionally, internal bank transactions, intercompany lending, and employee loans are not
subject to the DSCR minimums outlined herein unless explicitly stated otherwise in the parent policy or related documentation."""^^xsd:string ;
    cpi:version "3.1"^^xsd:string .

